@crew esposito-yara
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Esposito, crew store. Eight till half two. You'll need soap. Everyone does.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. You're out of toothpaste. Don't ask how I know.   #funny
- {hi}. New biscuits in. They'll be gone by nine.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I put one aside for you. Don't tell the queue.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good morning. Shelves full by eight. Guessed six orders right. Personal best.
? mood:low
- Slow morning. Restocked the full shelves. Don't look at me like that.

== near
? act:work
- Let me guess. Socks. No? Tea. I knew it was tea.   #funny
? act:gym
- Gym after shift. Stops me buying biscuits. Mostly.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I shop at my own store on my tea break. It's still shopping. Shush.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I keep a journal of every star I've seen. Wen and Farah keep one too. Mine's neater.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Best bit of the job? Guessing what people came in for. I'm right four times in five.

== about
? aff:ishikawa-orla:friend
- Orla does evenings, I do mornings. We leave each other notes. Very proper ones.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. Doors open. Socks on the left, soap on the right, gossip at the till.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. Half an hour till Ishikawa takes over. Buy something now, I'll remember it.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Oh, look who's back. Your soap's been lonely. So's your toothpaste.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}. Come back when you run out. You will.
? tier>=friend
- See you, {me}. Good chat. Better than restocking. Much better.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Shelves full, till balanced, kettle on. A good morning.

== near
? act:gym
- Gym, then the store. It stops me eating the stock. Mostly.   #funny
? deck:4 act:leisure
- Common room. Feet up. Don't ask me where anything is. I'm off.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Same counter, a good few years. I love it. I wonder sometimes what else I'd love.
? tier>=friend
- I can guess what anyone came in for. Except you. You're a mystery. A small one.   #warm

== invite
? tier>=colleague time:afternoon
- Gym after my shift? You lift, I'll tell you who bought what. Not really.   #funny

== accept
- Can do. I'll be there.
== decline
- Can't, sorry. Stock-take. Very thrilling. Another time.
== missed
- You didn't come. I'll put it on your tab. Kidding. Mostly.   #funny
== birthday
? birthday:me
- My birthday. I bought myself a present. From me. At staff price.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I've put something by. No charge. Don't tell anyone.   #warm
== hint
- Got a minute? Not for shopping. Just a minute.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- You'll want the thermal socks. Trust me.
- Store's open. Gerald says hello.   #funny
- Ah, well. Back on the shelf.
- New stock. Old stock, newly dusted.   #funny
? act:work
- Next. I know what you're after.

== rumour
- I never say what anyone bought. Ever.
- Heard it at the counter. Not from me.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- You fetched it before I asked. That's my trick. I'm impressed.   #funny
? told:fav.lamp
- You fixed my lamp. I can see the till. And Gerald. Gerald's pleased.   #funny
? told:fixed.lights
- Lights on Deck 3 are steady. Was that you? Thought so. You've got the look.
? told:came.running
- Saw you at running club. You'll want better socks. I've got some.   #funny
? told:gift.star
- That's going in my star journal. Page of its own. Thank you.   #warm
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday. I'll pretend I didn't notice. I noticed.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- Store's heard good things. People buy you biscuits. I notice. I never say who.   #funny
? you:kind
- You're known for being kind. I can tell by what you buy. Mostly for other people.   #warm
? you:chatty
- You chat to everyone at my counter. The queue's longer. I don't mind.
